+++ b/apps/web/src/guide/pages/stream-deck.mdx
+Profiles come with it, laid out for each deck (Stream Deck, Mini, XL and +). The Runlog profile installs with the plugin. A pack's profile has that pack's moves on keys, its counters and resources on the numbers, and its setups ready to hand out; it arrives the first time your deck follows a run of that pack, and the deck switches to it. **Switch to the pack's profile when a run attaches**, in Connect's settings, turns that off. A pack Runlog ships no profile for, one you bought or wrote yourself, gets one built from the run the first time your deck follows it: the plugin lays it out from what the run publishes, the same way it would from the pack file, and the Stream Deck app asks whether to import it. The deck stands on the Runlog profile until you say yes. A pack from the Marketplace also has its profile on its page, under **Stream Deck profile**: pick your deck, and import the file in the Stream Deck app. Once a profile is yours you can rearrange it like any other.
+- **Open in the browser** opens one page in your default browser, picked in its settings: the run the deck is following, that run's dock, a new run, this guide, or the pack's rules. The guide opens whether or not the deck is connected. Its last setting, **This pack's profile**, opens no page: it builds a profile for the pack the deck is following, laid out for the deck the key is on, and hands it to the Stream Deck app to import. It works for any pack, one Runlog ships a profile for or not.
